---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>What is this site?</h1>
			<p>
				This site is a minimally-modified <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> write-up starter template.
				I'm using it to make my vulnhub write-ups easily navigable, and to give myself an ongoing project.
			</p>
			<p>
			At the moment, the site is very basic. It shows my recent write-ups on a page, and then displays them the
				default template layout. I plan to add more features, such as a search box, filtering based off series
				and difficulty, and more displayed information when browsing the write-ups.
			</p>
			<p>Here are a few ideas on how to get started with the template:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Edit this page in <code>src/pages/index.astro</code></li>
				<li>Edit the site header items in <code>src/components/Header.astro</code></li>
				<li>Add your name to the footer in <code>src/components/Footer.astro</code></li>
				<li>Check out the included write-ups in <code>src/content/write-ups/</code></li>
				<li>Customize the write-up page layout in <code>src/layouts/write-up.astro</code></li>
			</ul>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
